---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii1_200",
  "series": "Band II 1 (1663 - 1685)",
  "seq": 200,
  "text": "<p> [[634.11]] <b>182. LEIBNIZ AN VINCENT PLACCIUS</p>\n<p> [[634.12]] [Anfang Juli 1678.] [178.185.]</b></p>\n<p> [[634.19]] Nobilissime et Consultissime Domine, Fautor Honoratissime. </p>\n<p> [[634.20]] Scripseram Webero, ut tibi pecuniam a me debitam solveret, idque nunc repetii ut praestet\n[[634.21]] in moneta apud vos probata. Plurimum interea tibi debeo, tum eo nomine, tum quod Fogelianae\n[[634.22]] Bibliothecae Catalogum misisti; quem recte accepi. De Conringianorum operum editione nihil\n[[634.23]] mihi auditum; etsi subinde ab ipso Conringio literas accipiam. </p>\n<p> [[634.24]] Spero me his diebus ad vos excurrere posse, ubi alloquio tuo frui, et inter alia de\n[[634.25]] Fogelianis et Jungianis loqui gestio. Recte sentis non nimis diu differendam meditationum non\n[[634.26]] vulgarium editionem: neque illos probo qui nimis in hoc genere sunt morosi. Neque sperandum\n[[635.1]] est enim quicquam a nobis edi posse ita omnibus absolutum numeris, ut postea nihil corrigendum\n[[635.2]] occurrat. Satis est ita a nobis scribi, ut post decennium, si vivimus, scripsisse non\n[[635.3]] poeniteat. Quod unum ego imposterum me curaturum innuebam. Nam quae olim scripsi vix\n[[635.4]] scholas egressus scripsisse fere poenitet. Nunc vero non pauca dare possem melioris ut spero\n[[635.5]] notae, si otium esset elaborandi. </p>\n<p> [[635.6]] In jurisprudentia id ago ut omnia revocentur ad pauca capita, quae qui teneat, caetera per\n[[635.7]] consequentiam certam inde ducere possit. Quod mihi videtur esse, jus ex infinito finitum\n[[635.8]] reddere. Quoniam autem saepe controversiae sunt circa ipsa fundamenta ex quibus caetera\n[[635.9]] ducenda essent, eas controversias velut Imperatoriae definitioni servandas annoto: illas praesertim\n[[635.10]] quibus dubitatur utrum Leges Romanae quaedam adhuc serventur. </p>\n<p> [[635.11]] In re Mathematica non pauca habeo quae a Viris etiam in hoc genere summis desiderari\n[[635.12]] accepi. Et quidem Parisiis reliqui scriptum edendum <i>de Quadratura Circuli et Hyperbolae\n[[635.13]] Arithmetica ejusque Corollario: <b>Trigonometria sine Tabulis.</b></i> Nam hic est maximus\n[[635.14]] Geometriae defectus, quod ex datis trianguli lateribus, vel ex datis angulis et uno latere, aut ex\n[[635.15]] duobus lateribus et uno angulo; reliqua non possunt inveniri hactenus per regulam constantem;\n[[635.16]] sed opus est tabulis jam calculatis. Itaque si quis in itinere opus haberet resolutione quadam\n[[635.17]] Trigonometrica, librisque careret, cogeretur unius exempli in numeris accuratis solvendi causa\n[[635.18]] immensum laborem subire, integramque velut Tabulam sibi condere. Huic defectui remedium\n[[635.19]] inveni et regulas duas exhibui, quarum una generaliter exhibet modum ex dato angulo vel arcu\n[[635.20]] inveniendi sinum, altera modum ex dato sinu inveniendi arcum vel angulum, idque exiguo\n[[635.21]] labore et in numeris quantumlibet exactis. Harum regularum demonstrationes examinavere\n[[635.22]] mathematici nostri temporis primarii, et veras deprehendere; sed etiam exactissimo calculo in\n[[635.23]] exemplis quibusdam inito veritatem expertus sum. Alia in his studiis inventa nunc memorare\n[[635.24]] omitto, quia non aeque sunt publici usus. </p>\n<p> [[635.25]] In Physicis habeo regulas motus perfectissime constitutas, et Archimedeo plane rigore\n[[635.26]] demonstratas. Si quis enim illis contradicat, eum redigere possum ad absurdum. Itaque valde\n[[635.27]] vellem videre an Jungianae consentiant. </p>\n<p> [[635.28]] Mechanica quaedam nunc memorare nihil attinet. </p>\n<p> [[635.29]] In penitiore philosophia multa dicenda haberem, certo demonstrata, et longe a quibusdam\n[[635.30]] Aristotelis aut Cartesii aut Hobbesii sententiis diversa, tametsi plurima ab illis tradita plane\n[[636.1]] probem. Sed cum haec studia pauci tractent, quid attinet scribere non legenda. Satis igitur\n[[636.2]] habebo aliquando circa Deum atque animam aliqua dare firma et ut spero profutura. </p>\n<p> [[636.3]] In Theologicis quoque non sum inexercitatus, nam jamdudum cum magnis viris de\n[[636.4]] religione contuli, epistolasque scripsi et accepi quae si ederentur forte nonnullas quaestiones\n[[636.5]] illustrarent. Sed ego literarum mearum exempla retinere non soleo, nisi cum singularis quaedam\n[[636.6]] ratio jubet. Intelligi tamen potest ex aliorum ad me literis, quam uberes fuerint meae. </p>\n<p> [[636.7]] Habes, Vir Cl^#'m^#'e nonnullas molitiones meas, quas nosse voluisti. Obsecutus sum mandato\n[[636.8]] tuo potius quam consilio meo neque enim prudentis est promittere quae praestitum iri in incerto\n[[636.9]] est. </p>\n<p> [[636.10]] Nescio cujus sit politica illa in quam commentatus est Clasenius, curabo tamen ut sciam. </p>\n<p> [[636.11]] Circa illam <i>immortalitatis animae demonstrationem</i> quam mihi transmiseras, et de qua\n[[636.12]] sententiam exposui, recte notas mecum resolvi denique debere in generale argumentum de\n[[636.13]] providentia seu justitia Dei. Digbaeus multa argumenta recenset, accurate tamen nihil demonstrat.\n[[636.14]] Claubergius est Cartesii paraphrastes. Cartesius egregia quidem attulit, demonstrationem\n[[636.15]] tamen non absolvit. Duo sunt diversa, immaterialitas animae, et immortalitas. Demonstrandum\n[[636.16]] est ergo 1.) ex metaphysicis, animam cum corpore non dissolvi, 2.) ex moralibus, animam in\n[[636.17]] alia vita et cogitare et meminisse. Neutrum debito rigore demonstratum est. Sed finiendi tempus\n[[636.18]] est. Vale faveque </p>\n<p> [[636.19]] Nobilissime Domine Tibi deditissimo Leibnitio. </p>\n",
  "number": "182.",
  "title": "LEIBNIZ AN VINCENT PLACCIUS",
  "date": "[Anfang Juli 1678.] [178.185.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:182. LEIBNIZ AN VINCENT PLACCIUS [Anfang Juli 1678.] [178.185.] Nobilissime et Consultissime Domine, Fautor Honoratissime. Scripseram Webero, ut tibi pecuniam a me debitam solveret, idque nunc repetii ut praestet in moneta apud vos probata. Plurimum interea tibi debeo, tum eo nomine, tum quod Fogeli...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>